title: 'pallet-validator-collators: relay-chain validators as system chain collators'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `pallet-validator-collators`, a second session manager for system chains. It stores
    the active validator set of each era and returns its validators with registered keys as
    collators, next to `pallet-collator-selection` through `UnionSessionManager`, a new
    combinator in `pallet-session` that merges the sets of two session managers. A new set
    forces two session rotations so it takes effect within two blocks. On Asset Hub the
    pallet also sends the set to the other system chains, with retries.

    `pallet-staking-async` gains the `OnEraStart` config item, called with the validators of
    each era when it becomes active. Use `()` to keep the previous behaviour at no cost.

    Asset Hub Westend and People Westend use the new pallet. Asset Hub announces every new
    era to itself and to People. The pallet and call index of People's `set_validators` are
    hard-coded on Asset Hub, and the two runtimes share the validator bound.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
# `OnEraStart` is a new required config item and `NextEraValidators` is new storage.
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: major
- name: pallet-session
  bump: minor
# Adding the pallet changes the runtimes' public `PalletInstancesInfo` type.
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: testnet-parachains-constants
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: none
- name: pallet-ahm-test
  bump: none
- name: people-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: minor
